From 389e7e969bd0626419fe9f16efb458c10789ddc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TofuJoe <darryl.hon@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 10:31:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 32/32] drm/xe/display: Don't reserve the BO on ADDFB2 when
 FORCE_WC is already set

xe_display_bo_framebuffer_init() took the BO's reservation on every ADDFB2
only to set XE_BO_FLAG_FORCE_WC, which scanout BOs already carry from
creation and which is never cleared. Mutter creates a framebuffer per frame
on the same swapchain BO it is rendering into, so the ww-mutex contended
with the client's exec for nothing. Test the flag first and only lock when
it is actually missing (the original path, unchanged).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/display/xe_display_bo.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/display/xe_display_bo.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/display/xe_display_bo.c
index f8aaba8..37104e7 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/display/xe_display_bo.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/display/xe_display_bo.c
@@ -64,6 +64,16 @@ static int xe_display_bo_framebuffer_init(struct drm_gem_object *obj,
 
 	xe_bo_get(bo);
 
+	/*
+	 * XE_BO_FLAG_FORCE_WC is only ever set, never cleared, and scanout BOs
+	 * carry it from creation. The compositor creates a framebuffer for
+	 * every frame, so don't take the BO's reservation (which contends with
+	 * its own exec on the same swapchain BO) just to find the flag set.
+	 */
+	if ((READ_ONCE(bo->flags) & XE_BO_FLAG_FORCE_WC) ||
+	    bo->ttm.type == ttm_bo_type_sg)
+		return 0;
+
 	ret = ttm_bo_reserve(&bo->ttm, true, false, NULL);
 	if (ret)
 		goto err;
